from scripts.curate_remaining import Batch
b=Batch('01-computing',['Mathematics','Computer Science','Cryptography','Quantum Computing','Machine Learning','Software Engineering','Human-Computer Interaction','Computer Engineering']);a=b.a;u=b.u
# Explicitly scoped engineering routes rather than mathematical-conjecture chains.
a('CRY-09','CRY-03','A new hardness assumption with an obfuscation construction could supply a candidate foundation for the proposed program obfuscator.','An assumption alone is not a construction or a proof of security; efficiency and the exact security definition still need work.','enabling')
a('CRY-04','CRY-08','Succinct proofs could let an outsourcing client check a computation result without repeating the full computation.','An NP proof system does not by itself establish the target’s general program model, minimal overhead or information-theoretic security.','enabling')
a('CSC-03','HCI-07','Encrypted computation could be investigated as a way to process interaction data without exposing plaintext to the processor.','Ciphertext processing does not settle consent, metadata leakage, usable controls or zero cognitive burden.','enabling')
a('CRY-05','HCI-07','Joint computation on private inputs could support an interaction design that shares results rather than raw user data.','The source’s constant-communication ambition is unverified; a protocol does not establish effortless privacy or every privacy guarantee.','enabling')
a('CRY-07','HCI-10','A long-term data-protection scheme could contribute to the security of a lifelong external memory archive.','Long-term confidentiality would not supply memory integration, recall accuracy or cognitive benefit.')
a('CRY-10','QUA-05','A quantum-era limits framework could test whether a candidate encrypted-quantum-computation design fits its claimed security model.','A bound may rule out a design rather than provide a practical scheme; no particular bound or construction is asserted here.')
a('CRY-10','CRY-07','Limits on quantum cryptographic models could help specify which long-term adversary assumptions an everlasting-security proposal must address.','This does not establish that the stated unbounded-adversary protection is achievable.')
a('QUA-02','CSC-04','An ambient-temperature coherent qubit platform could be one hardware route to investigate fault-tolerant scaling.','Single-platform fidelity would not establish large-scale integration or millions of logical qubits.','alternative-route',group='fault-tolerant-platforms')
a('QUA-06','CSC-04','A topological-qubit platform could be another hardware route to investigate error-corrected scaling.','Protected qubits do not by themselves establish manufacture, logical gates or large-system error rates. Routes may combine.','alternative-route',group='fault-tolerant-platforms')
a('QUA-09','QUA-04','A suitable quantum memory could hold a network state while a proposed repeater system establishes other links.','The network need not use the source’s ambient self-correcting memory; rate, loss and entanglement operations remain separate.')
a('CSC-04','QUA-03','An error-corrected computer could provide an execution and validation setting for a proposed optimization algorithm.','The algorithm could be discovered first; millions of logical qubits are not asserted necessary and an exponential advantage is not established.')
a('CSC-04','QUA-08','An error-corrected system could provide a test setting for a proposed quantum-learning algorithm.','Hardware availability does not establish a classical-data speedup or remove data-loading costs.')
a('CSC-04','QUA-07','A fault-tolerant system could execute candidate chemically accurate simulation algorithms.','The target mentions hundreds of logical qubits, so the much larger source computer is an optional resource, not a prerequisite.')
a('QUA-07','CHM-09','A chemically accurate quantum-simulation method could be one computational route to explore the chemistry target.','Chemical accuracy for selected systems is narrower than an exact, routine solution for all large molecules.','alternative-route',group='molecular-computation')
a('MLC-04','MLC-08','Mechanistic explanations could make a candidate safety argument’s assumptions and internal failure modes more inspectable.','An explanation does not define human values or prove alignment under all future inputs and self-modifications.')
a('MLC-04','MLC-10','Inspectable computational mechanisms could help test how proposed cognitive components interact in an integrated architecture.','Understanding a trained model does not establish general intelligence or a single universal architecture.')
a('MLC-05','MLC-07','A learning rule with lower training energy could contribute to the proposed energy budget.','Lower energy for a tested workload would not establish the brain-comparable throughput and power claimed by the original ambition.')
a('MLC-06','MLC-10','A causal-planning component could be investigated within a proposed integrated cognitive architecture.','It is one architectural option; causal reasoning alone does not establish all cognitive capabilities.','enabling')
a('MLC-02','HCI-04','A continual learner could update a personalized interface while retaining earlier preferences.','Retention is not correct anticipation, consent or zero effort, and a complete lifelong-learning solution is not necessary for every adaptive interface.','enabling')
a('HCI-04','HCI-06','Adaptation mechanisms could be used to test individualized presentation and control for particular accessibility needs.','Perfect anticipation and universal accessibility are not assumed; inclusion requires explicit user evaluation.')
a('HCI-05','HCI-08','A haptic channel could add tactile feedback to a proposed remote shared environment.','Haptics do not provide all sensory cues or establish experience indistinguishable from physical co-location.','enabling')
a('HCI-02','HCI-08','A visual overlay could provide a display route for a proposed shared spatial environment.','Contact lenses are not required; display realism does not supply audio, gaze, latency or physical presence.','enabling')
a('CPE-01','MLC-07','Lower-switching-energy devices could be a hardware-led approach to reducing learning-system power.','Device-level efficiency need not translate to the whole workload or the source’s throughput target.','alternative-route',group='efficient-learning-hardware')
a('CPE-05','MLC-07','A photonic-electronic design could be investigated to reduce conversion or interconnect energy in learning workloads.','Zero-latency and lossless conversion remain aspirations; total system energy could fail to improve.','alternative-route',group='efficient-learning-hardware')
a('CPE-09','MLC-07','A cooled computing stack could be investigated as another hardware approach to reducing computation energy.','Cooling overhead and workload behavior could negate device savings; the stated power target is not implied.','alternative-route',group='efficient-learning-hardware')
a('CPE-08','CPE-10','Reconfigurable circuits could provide hardware configurations for executing extracted parallel work.','Rewiring does not find all parallelism or verify that a transformation preserves semantics.','enabling')
a('SWE-02','CPE-10','Verification methods could supply proof obligations for automatically parallelized execution.','A broad software-verification framework is not necessary for every hardware proof, and it does not remove runtime overhead.','enabling')
a('CPE-06','SWE-05','A device trust primitive could anchor a proposed hardware/software assurance chain.','Trusted hardware does not prevent software vulnerabilities or establish immunity to every attack.','enabling')
a('SWE-06','SWE-10','Maintainability estimates could help an engineering agent compare proposed changes and longer-term costs.','Forecasting code costs does not establish autonomous engineering performance.')
a('SWE-10','SWE-06','Logged changes and measured outcomes from a coding agent could provide additional examples for testing maintainability models.','This is a proposed evidence-collection feedback loop; generated changes may be biased and do not establish predictive laws.','feedback')
a('SWE-03','SWE-04','Semantics-preserving transformations could constrain performance optimization in a self-modifying runtime.','Preserving existing semantics cannot by itself correct wrong behavior; no never-crash or zero-regression guarantee follows.')
a('SWE-09','SWE-10','Task-complexity bounds could help an engineering agent recognize infeasible searches or compare algorithmic budgets.','Bounds alone do not produce the best implementation or a universal engineering agent.')
a('CSC-09','SWE-09','Explicit lower-bound techniques could contribute examples and methods to a broader complexity framework for software tasks.','A circuit separation does not determine every software architecture or algorithmic optimum.')
a('CSC-10','SWE-09','Fine-grained reductions could help compare the conditional difficulty of specified software problems.','Conditional bounds remain assumption-dependent and do not establish a complete predictive theory.')
for id,reason in {
'MAT-01':'A zeta-zero theorem is a foundational result. The collection supplies no specific downstream construction whose capability follows from this statement.',
'MAT-02':'Either answer to P versus NP has different consequences; a resolution alone need not provide a practical solver. No unconditional capability arrow is justified.',
'MAT-03':'Existence and regularity of 3D solutions do not themselves supply a fast numerical solver or turbulence control. A concrete computational mechanism is missing.',
'MAT-04':'No target in this collection specifies an algorithm or device whose construction follows from the stated algebraic-cycle result.',
'MAT-05':'The rank/L-function identity alone does not supply a concrete capability in the collection; a constructive downstream method is unspecified.',
'MAT-06':'Existence and a mass gap do not directly provide a usable chemistry or engineering model. No specific application mechanism is established by the source.',
'MAT-07':'The integer iteration conjecture has no described engineering or scientific target in the collection that would be enabled by its resolution.',
'MAT-08':'The prime-sum existence statement supplies no specified constructive capability or prerequisite for another listed milestone.',
'MAT-09':'Infinitely many prime pairs do not directly supply the secure primitives listed here; a number-theory-to-cryptography arrow would be speculative without a construction.',
'MAT-10':'A perfect-number existence result has no concrete downstream capability specified in these source entries.',
'CSC-01':'Source explicitly flags equivalence to MAT-02. Retain that metadata; a duplicate is not a causal prerequisite.',
'CSC-02':'A one-way-function construction alone does not establish the advanced primitives, quantum security or efficiency targets here. A suitable reduction and adversary model are unspecified.',
'CSC-05':'Fast matrix multiplication has broad possible uses, but no listed target provides a specific bottleneck and end-to-end improvement argument. A generic faster-compute arrow was rejected.',
'CSC-06':'An approximation-hardness resolution does not itself provide the efficient capabilities listed here; no justified constructive pathway was identified.',
'CSC-07':'A statement about physical simulation limits is not a new computational device or algorithm. No concrete capability direction is justified without the theorem’s outcome.',
'CRY-01':'The source flags equivalence to CSC-03; preserve the duplicate relationship without inventing a dependency.',
'CRY-02':'No listed implementation platform or hardness construction establishes the simultaneous security, key-size and speed target; related signature goals overlap rather than cause it.',
'CRY-06':'This is a specialized post-quantum signature ambition. The broader public-key ambition is overlapping scope, not a demonstrated enabling mechanism.',
'QUA-01':'Source flags equivalence to CSC-04. Keep its original entry and canonical reference, not a causal arrow between equivalent goals.',
'QUA-10':'The desired new computational model is unspecified; naming algorithm families does not justify a directional link to a particular unproved speedup.',
'HCI-01':'No reviewed input in this batch supplies non-invasive single-neuron read/write access. An implanted neural interface would not solve the non-invasive requirement.',
'HCI-03':'The source combines perfect mental-state inference with zero privacy intrusion. No justified measurement and privacy mechanism was identified; no achievement is assumed.',
'HCI-09':'A universal symbiosis theory does not identify a concrete intervention or testable downstream construction in the collection.'
}.items():u(id,reason,'source-equivalence' if id in ['CSC-01','CRY-01','QUA-01'] else 'unresolved-mechanism')
b.reject('MAT-02','CSC-03','A P-versus-NP resolution alone is neither a practical encryption construction nor a secure outcome guarantee.')
b.reject('BME-02','HCI-01','An invasive interface is not an enabling solution for the explicitly non-invasive sensing requirement.')
b.branch('quantum-platforms','Quantum platforms and simulation',['QUA-02','QUA-06','CSC-04','QUA-07','CHM-09','QUA-03','QUA-08'])
b.branch('private-interaction','Private computation and interaction',['CRY-09','CRY-03','CRY-04','CRY-08','CSC-03','CRY-05','HCI-07','CRY-07','HCI-10'])
b.branch('runtime-feedback','Runtime and engineering feedback',['SWE-02','SWE-01','SWE-03','SWE-04','SWE-06','SWE-10','SWE-09','CSC-10'])
b.save()
